  "id": "ffc2c5ba-5c36-4ef4-818b-5646462477aa",
  "title": "Digital Personal Data Protection Act and Its Impact on Press Freedom",
  "summary": "The Hindu National reports that the Digital Personal Data Protection Act does not infringe on press freedom, while Business Standard highlights that the act does not curb press freedom, citing concerns from news publishers. The government seeks to engage with media professionals to discuss the implications of the law.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Indian government has announced the Digital Personal Data Protection Act (DPDP Act) as a measure to protect personal data, but it does not infringe on press freedom.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "A day after news publishers challenged the act, the government reiterated its commitment to protecting press freedom in the context of the law.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The act aims to balance data protection with the need to safeguard journalistic integrity and freedom of expression.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
